1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,469
On Thursday, a company that reported an eighty billion dollar loss in six months is going public.

2
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:13,710
Investors want it so badly that orders are running at about six times the shares for sale.

3
00:00:14,099 --> 00:00:16,309
The company is Anthropic.

4
00:00:16,339 --> 00:00:18,989
It makes an AI model called Claude.

5
00:00:19,219 --> 00:00:25,190
And at the top of its price range, it would be worth one point four trillion dollars.

6
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:29,309
Here is why this matters even if you never buy a single share.

7
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:37,390
Within a few weeks, some of the biggest index funds in America may have to buy it, at whatever price it happens to be trading.

8
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:40,869
One of them could be in your retirement account.

9
00:00:40,899 --> 00:00:44,990
And the biggest winners of this deal are not the people buying on Thursday.

10
00:00:45,219 --> 00:00:47,310
They were decided years ago.

11
00:00:48,124 --> 00:00:49,253
One quick note.

12
00:00:49,484 --> 00:00:55,533
This was recorded a few days before the shares started trading, so the final price may differ.

13
00:00:55,564 --> 00:00:59,334
Every number you are about to see has its source on screen.

14
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:02,273
Start with the deal itself.

15
00:01:02,302 --> 00:01:08,953
Anthropic is selling eight hundred and twenty-five million shares, at seventy to seventy-eight dollars each.

16
00:01:09,343 --> 00:01:12,873
That would raise up to sixty-four billion dollars.

17
00:01:12,942 --> 00:01:19,673
Reports call it the second largest stock market debut in history, behind SpaceX earlier this year.

18
00:01:19,903 --> 00:01:21,433
Now, the valuation.

19
00:01:21,742 --> 00:01:25,753
You will see two numbers in the headlines, and both are real.

20
00:01:25,822 --> 00:01:31,673
Count only the shares that exist today, and Anthropic is worth about one trillion dollars.

21
00:01:31,983 --> 00:01:38,552
Count every share that has been promised to employees and investors, and you get one point four trillion.

22
00:01:38,623 --> 00:01:43,992
Either way, it is less than the two trillion that was being whispered a few months ago.

23
00:01:43,942 --> 00:01:45,033
Remember that.

24
00:01:44,822 --> 00:01:46,233
We will come back to it.

25
00:01:47,036 --> 00:01:49,085
Now, that loss.

26
00:01:49,115 --> 00:01:55,445
In the first half of this year, Anthropic brought in sixteen point three billion dollars in revenue.

27
00:01:55,756 --> 00:02:00,046
And it reported a net loss of eighty point seven billion.

28
00:02:00,075 --> 00:02:02,325
That sounds like a company on fire.

29
00:02:02,555 --> 00:02:04,126
It is not.

30
00:02:04,156 --> 00:02:09,045
About seventy-two billion dollars of that loss is an accounting charge.

31
00:02:09,116 --> 00:02:13,205
Anthropic had borrowed money using notes that convert into shares.

32
00:02:13,436 --> 00:02:18,645
When the company became more valuable, those notes became more expensive on paper.

33
00:02:18,955 --> 00:02:20,645
No cash left the building.

34
00:02:21,036 --> 00:02:27,205
Strip that out, and the loss from actually running the business was under seven hundred million dollars.

35
00:02:27,436 --> 00:02:32,006
In its most recent reported quarter, Anthropic made an operating profit.

36
00:02:32,395 --> 00:02:34,406
So is it safe?

37
00:02:34,235 --> 00:02:34,806
No.

38
00:02:35,195 --> 00:02:36,725
Here is the other side.

39
00:02:36,955 --> 00:02:39,925
To run AI, you need computing power.

40
00:02:40,156 --> 00:02:44,725
Anthropic spent nearly nine billion dollars on it in six months.

41
00:02:44,955 --> 00:02:48,086
That is more than it spent in all of last year.

42
00:02:48,156 --> 00:02:51,605
And it has signed contracts to keep spending for years.

43
00:02:51,915 --> 00:02:58,885
One analysis of the filing puts its commitment to Google alone above one hundred and twenty billion dollars.

44
00:02:59,276 --> 00:03:00,566
That is the bet.

45
00:03:00,795 --> 00:03:04,406
Revenue has to keep growing faster than the bills.

46
00:03:05,223 --> 00:03:07,393
So what does this company sell?

47
00:03:07,703 --> 00:03:09,832
Not a chatbot for the public.

48
00:03:09,862 --> 00:03:12,193
Most people have never used Claude.

49
00:03:12,423 --> 00:03:15,712
Anthropic's money comes mainly from businesses.

50
00:03:15,782 --> 00:03:24,353
Banks, software companies, and law firms pay to run Claude inside their own products, and they pay by how much they use it.

51
00:03:24,502 --> 00:03:27,193
And they are using a lot more.

52
00:03:27,223 --> 00:03:33,953
According to the filing, customers who were paying a year ago are now spending about nine times as much.

53
00:03:34,263 --> 00:03:38,112
Revenue in the second quarter was more than double the first quarter.

54
00:03:38,342 --> 00:03:39,872
Not double in a year.

55
00:03:40,022 --> 00:03:42,112
Double in three months.

56
00:03:42,502 --> 00:03:45,552
That is the number behind the trillion dollar price.

57
00:03:45,943 --> 00:03:49,393
Growth like that is almost unheard of at this size.

58
00:03:49,782 --> 00:03:52,513
The question is how long it can last.

59
00:03:52,742 --> 00:03:56,673
Because growth that fast usually means one of two things.

60
00:03:56,983 --> 00:03:59,592
Either a new industry is being born.

61
00:03:59,622 --> 00:04:04,432
Or customers are experimenting with money they will not keep spending.

62
00:04:05,229 --> 00:04:09,278
Which brings us to the company everyone expected to go first.

63
00:04:09,308 --> 00:04:10,639
OpenAI.

64
00:04:10,588 --> 00:04:13,038
The maker of ChatGPT.

65
00:04:13,149 --> 00:04:20,598
This month, OpenAI went to investors asking for a valuation of one point four trillion dollars.

66
00:04:20,668 --> 00:04:24,079
According to reports, investors pushed back.

67
00:04:24,108 --> 00:04:27,478
It settled for one point two five trillion.

68
00:04:27,269 --> 00:04:32,678
And it raised about fifteen billion dollars, roughly half of what it wanted.

69
00:04:32,548 --> 00:04:34,278
Why the pushback?

70
00:04:34,108 --> 00:04:44,759
The Wall Street Journal reported that last quarter, OpenAI took in six point seven billion dollars, and lost twelve point three billion running the business.

71
00:04:44,588 --> 00:04:48,759
For every dollar it earned, it lost almost two.

72
00:04:48,588 --> 00:04:53,639
OpenAI's own stock market debut has now been pushed to next year.

73
00:04:53,468 --> 00:05:00,119
So for the first time, the smaller rival may be valued higher than the company that started the boom.

74
00:05:00,028 --> 00:05:03,238
That is the story Wall Street is telling this week.

75
00:05:03,069 --> 00:05:06,199
Keep in mind who benefits from that story.

76
00:05:06,028 --> 00:05:10,439
A company about to sell sixty-four billion dollars of stock.

77
00:05:11,244 --> 00:05:13,653
Now the part most headlines skip.

78
00:05:13,483 --> 00:05:14,774
Google.

79
00:05:14,603 --> 00:05:18,213
Google competes with both of these companies.

80
00:05:18,084 --> 00:05:22,134
Its own AI, Gemini, has a billion users.

81
00:05:21,963 --> 00:05:25,653
But Google also owns a large piece of Anthropic.

82
00:05:25,483 --> 00:05:29,413
Estimates range from about ten to fourteen percent.

83
00:05:29,244 --> 00:05:35,494
At the middle of the price range, that stake is worth around one hundred and thirty billion dollars.

84
00:05:35,324 --> 00:05:38,533
And Google sells Anthropic the chips it runs on.

85
00:05:38,363 --> 00:05:40,454
Up to a million of them.

86
00:05:40,283 --> 00:05:46,213
Google's cloud business more than doubled last quarter, to over thirty billion dollars.

87
00:05:46,043 --> 00:05:47,413
Think about that.

88
00:05:47,244 --> 00:05:50,853
If Anthropic wins, Google's shares go up.

89
00:05:50,684 --> 00:05:54,374
If Anthropic spends heavily, Google gets the money.

90
00:05:54,163 --> 00:05:58,533
And if Anthropic loses, Google still has Gemini.

91
00:05:58,363 --> 00:06:00,894
Amazon is in the same position.

92
00:06:00,684 --> 00:06:10,747
It is Anthropic's other giant shareholder, with a stake valued at around one hundred and forty billion dollars, and it sells Anthropic computing power too.

93
00:06:10,550 --> 00:06:12,774
And they are not alone.

94
00:06:12,603 --> 00:06:20,574
Alongside the public sale, about twenty-six billion dollars of stock is being sold directly to a small group of companies.

95
00:06:20,363 --> 00:06:26,507
Reports name Microsoft, Nvidia, Alphabet, and the chip maker Micron.

96
00:06:26,310 --> 00:06:28,173
Look at that list again.

97
00:06:27,963 --> 00:06:32,973
Those are the companies that sell Anthropic its chips and its computing power.

98
00:06:32,764 --> 00:06:36,093
They are buying shares in their own customer.

99
00:06:35,884 --> 00:06:40,093
If you watched our first video, you have seen this loop before.

100
00:06:39,884 --> 00:06:45,173
The money goes around in a circle, and everyone in the circle reports growth.

101
00:06:45,043 --> 00:06:48,266
Those are the winners that were decided years ago.

102
00:06:48,071 --> 00:06:52,774
They bought in early, and they get paid on the way in and on the way out.

103
00:06:53,593 --> 00:06:55,923
One more thing the filing tells you.

104
00:06:55,913 --> 00:06:57,524
Who is in charge.

105
00:06:57,913 --> 00:07:03,603
Last week we told you how Nvidia's founder could be removed, because he had no special shares.

106
00:07:03,913 --> 00:07:05,923
Anthropic is the opposite.

107
00:07:06,153 --> 00:07:09,843
Its seven founders own about thirteen percent of the company.

108
00:07:10,153 --> 00:07:15,043
But through a special class of shares, they hold just over half of the votes.

109
00:07:15,353 --> 00:07:19,444
Amazon and Google, for all their money, have no vote at all.

110
00:07:19,834 --> 00:07:21,843
And the people buying on Thursday?

111
00:07:22,074 --> 00:07:25,124
Together, they get about six percent of the company.

112
00:07:25,514 --> 00:07:29,283
You may think founder control is a good thing or a bad thing.

113
00:07:29,434 --> 00:07:31,764
But know that it is the deal.

114
00:07:31,994 --> 00:07:35,444
If you own this stock, you are a passenger.

115
00:07:36,254 --> 00:07:43,144
Before you decide anything, look at what happened the last few times the whole country wanted the same stock.

116
00:07:43,615 --> 00:07:45,625
Facebook, 2012.

117
00:07:45,855 --> 00:07:48,824
The most anticipated debut of its era.

118
00:07:49,134 --> 00:07:51,704
It went public at thirty-eight dollars.

119
00:07:51,935 --> 00:07:55,785
Within four months it had lost more than half its value.

120
00:07:56,014 --> 00:07:59,865
It took over a year just to get back to the starting price.

121
00:08:00,334 --> 00:08:02,185
Uber, 2019.

122
00:08:02,415 --> 00:08:04,584
Priced at forty-five dollars.

123
00:08:04,814 --> 00:08:10,904
It fell on its very first day, and spent most of the next year and a half below that price.

124
00:08:11,454 --> 00:08:14,345
Both companies went on to be worth far more.

125
00:08:14,654 --> 00:08:18,345
Facebook is now one of the most valuable companies on earth.

126
00:08:18,814 --> 00:08:22,305
So the lesson is not that these were bad businesses.

127
00:08:22,334 --> 00:08:28,425
The lesson is that the first day is usually the most expensive day to be excited.

128
00:08:28,254 --> 00:08:32,504
The people who did best were not the ones who bought the debut.

129
00:08:32,335 --> 00:08:38,105
They were the ones who owned it before, and the ones who waited until the excitement had passed.

130
00:08:39,004 --> 00:08:41,214
So what does this mean for you?

131
00:08:41,244 --> 00:08:43,653
It depends on which fund you own.

132
00:08:43,724 --> 00:08:47,333
Earlier this year, Nasdaq changed its rules.

133
00:08:47,203 --> 00:08:53,974
A giant new company can now join the Nasdaq-100 index after just fifteen trading days.

134
00:08:53,964 --> 00:08:56,933
Before, the wait was at least three months.

135
00:08:57,004 --> 00:09:04,214
Reuters reports that Anthropic is likely to be added to several major indexes within five to fifteen days.

136
00:09:04,443 --> 00:09:09,494
When that happens, every fund that tracks those indexes has to buy the stock.

137
00:09:09,644 --> 00:09:12,134
They do not get to wait for a better price.

138
00:09:12,524 --> 00:09:21,813
When SpaceX went public in June, analysts estimated that index funds had to buy about fourteen billion dollars of its stock within three weeks.

139
00:09:21,964 --> 00:09:25,573
And only around five percent of the company was actually for sale.

140
00:09:25,964 --> 00:09:34,293
So if you own a Nasdaq-100 fund, or a total market fund, you will probably own a little Anthropic by the end of the year.

141
00:09:34,364 --> 00:09:37,813
But if you own an S&P 500 fund, you will not.

142
00:09:38,124 --> 00:09:40,374
That index kept its old rules.

143
00:09:40,443 --> 00:09:44,374
A company must be public for twelve months, and profitable.

144
00:09:44,604 --> 00:09:48,333
The earliest Anthropic could join is late next year.

145
00:09:48,524 --> 00:09:49,774
Same company.

146
00:09:49,724 --> 00:09:50,813
Same week.

147
00:09:50,764 --> 00:09:57,094
Two very different outcomes, depending on a line in your statement that most people have never read.

148
00:09:57,897 --> 00:10:00,067
So here is what to watch.

149
00:10:00,136 --> 00:10:00,947
One.

150
00:10:00,937 --> 00:10:02,866
The price on Wednesday night.

151
00:10:03,096 --> 00:10:07,586
If it lands at the top of the range, or above it, demand is real.

152
00:10:07,817 --> 00:10:12,386
If it lands at the bottom, the two trillion dollar whisper was the peak.

153
00:10:12,777 --> 00:10:13,626
Two.

154
00:10:13,657 --> 00:10:15,866
Where it closes on Thursday.

155
00:10:15,897 --> 00:10:21,506
Above one point two five trillion, and Anthropic is officially worth more than OpenAI.

156
00:10:21,817 --> 00:10:22,746
Three.

157
00:10:22,777 --> 00:10:23,907
Mid December.

158
00:10:24,216 --> 00:10:29,067
That is when the index decision is due, and when the forced buying would begin.

159
00:10:29,177 --> 00:10:33,346
Every boom has a moment when the public is finally invited in.

160
00:10:33,657 --> 00:10:36,067
Sometimes that moment is the beginning.

161
00:10:36,057 --> 00:10:37,907
Sometimes it is the top.

162
00:10:38,297 --> 00:10:43,907
The people who built this company, and the giants who funded it, have already been paid.

163
00:10:43,736 --> 00:10:47,746
On Thursday, it is your turn to decide what it is worth.
